{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "id": "msg_011Ch24oDjvCaJoeP6u7FPSk", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01XCfG32EnWBpsaDuSbQgGdQ", "name": "mcp__device__sign_off", "input": {"verdict": "PASS", "confidence": 0.55, "notes": "Sweep of sorting/grouping, subtasks, and task search on Tasks.org. Checked: sort direction toggles (sorting and grouping) update the sheet and list order and persist across HOME/relaunch; grouping by due date (Thu/Tue/Fri/No due date) and by start date (\"No start date\") render correctly; descending order reverses the list; subtask expand/collapse, completing a subtask with Undo, and the subtask badge with completed subtasks shown (2 of 2 with one completed); search matches title and notes, subtask matches, ranking follows the active sort (ascending and descending gave reversed orders), no-match shows empty state, and opening a result opens the right task. Restored the sort/grouping settings and task states to the starting data. One observation filed: the Pack for trip badge drops from 2 to 1 when 'Show completed subtasks' is off and one subtask is completed; the developer could not reproduce it, so it is unresolved and my confidence is moderate. Not tested: start-date grouping with real Today/Tomorrow/overdue start dates (would require editing task data), deeper subtask nesting (no nested data present), and landscape layout beyond a single rotation check. Also note the rotation to landscape showed the list in a narrow pane, which I did not file."}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 1253, "cache_read_input_tokens": 212632, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 1253}, "output_tokens": 24, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "32eaf94d-ea5c-4e4b-9f71-cfd087a4c3a8", "uuid": "758e9aaa-e2a0-4860-aada-2cb9284fa2fc", "timestamp": "2026-11-14T02:54:47.033Z", "request_id": "req_011Ch24oDUYRgaamGLQsvLL2", "wire_tool_inputs": {"toolu_01XCfG32EnWBpsaDuSbQgGdQ": {"verdict": "PASS", "confidence": 0.55, "notes": "Sweep of sorting/grouping, subtasks, and task search on Tasks.org. Checked: sort direction toggles (sorting and grouping) update the sheet and list order and persist across HOME/relaunch; grouping by due date (Thu/Tue/Fri/No due date) and by start date (\"No start date\") render correctly; descending order reverses the list; subtask expand/collapse, completing a subtask with Undo, and the subtask badge with completed subtasks shown (2 of 2 with one completed); search matches title and notes, subtask matches, ranking follows the active sort (ascending and descending gave reversed orders), no-match shows empty state, and opening a result opens the right task. Restored the sort/grouping settings and task states to the starting data. One observation filed: the Pack for trip badge drops from 2 to 1 when 'Show completed subtasks' is off and one subtask is completed; the developer could not reproduce it, so it is unresolved and my confidence is moderate. Not tested: start-date grouping with real Today/Tomorrow/overdue start dates (would require editing task data), deeper subtask nesting (no nested data present), and landscape layout beyond a single rotation check. Also note the rotation to landscape showed the list in a narrow pane, which I did not file."}}, "tool_use_meta": [{"id": "toolu_01XCfG32EnWBpsaDuSbQgGdQ", "display_name": "Sign Off", "server_display_name": "aqb-device", "tool_name": "sign_off"}]}
